Exactly one year ago, we released a Halloween-themed game demo.
Well, we decided that this tradition is worth keeping, and now we present you with a big autumn update!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/43681990/880892374b59ead0ff537f8448c5f62d195c8878.gif

It includes new quests, unique costumes for the witch, achievements, animated cutscenes, and even an intro. Many of these additions were inspired by player feedback, activities, and even contests. Need we say how grateful the The Witch's Cauldron team is to everyone who has supported us with advice, game purchases, and comments? So spend a little more time with our witch, explore where cooking and revenge can lead, find out what a succubus's love costs, and try to survive with limited ingredients or without hints from the book. The night will be long and dark—better stay close to the warm cauldron!

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/43681990/e2dda77ebc9f3086489f99c59b21dba1475e789a.gif

What’s included in the update:

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/43681990/7bdb5fe24a6569a84c9de4f78137d4e50737e6b8.png


 New characters with unique quests;
 Cloud saves;
 Animated cutscenes;
 A wardrobe for skins;
 Witch outfits, both selected from creative contests and made by us;
 New game modes that can be activated by choosing specific outfits;
 Premium skins for the witch and the cat, included in the supporter pack;
 A lore art book from the supporter pack.


https://store.steampowered.com/app/2955860/The_Witchs_Cauldron__Supporter_Pack/
{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/43681990/14b5e4530558650a720c8c4ca68ec79651e98497.jpg

And... this witch's story comes to an end. We’re not planning any more major updates, except possibly some cosmetic changes or a few archival quests. We're moving on to a new game—a sequel, if you will. In it, we aim to use all our accumulated knowledge and skills to make a game that’s even more vibrant, engaging, bigger, and deeper. So keep an eye on our social media—updates won’t be far behind.

{STEAM_CLAN_IMAGE}/43681990/cdc44b5bc54afd66a5e6c79d854a602b6d5fcb44.gif

Greetings, Potions Masters!

I want to inform you that already this summer we are ready to share with you a demo version of the game, in which you will find several branches of events and personal stories of characters who will definitely look at the light under your magic cauldron, because the rumor about the newly arrived healer and herbalist has already spread around the neighborhood.

https://cdna.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/062/465/288/large/harvey-games-base-backgroundshoot3-00109.jpg?1683198562
Our team, led by me, of course, carefully prepared and is now ready to show you the fruits of our labors:

https://cdnb.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/062/465/139/large/harvey-games-steam-up4.jpg?1683198063

– significantly improved the elements of the potion book: now you can see all the potions that are in the game, but not all of them will be available immediately – you will have to look for ways to get and use them;
- now I, Bobby the cat, will, from time to time, give you tips, as well as warnings about how we should act in this situation;
- each brewed potion has its own unique effect that distinguishes it from the rest;
– the division into cycles of day and night has become clear and have animations of their shifts: everyone knows that potions work well under the cover of night, and the fruits of your deeds make themselves felt the very next day;
- for lovers of reading, the witch has already compiled a guide to the ingredients and their properties;
- we, I - Bobby and the Witch, already keep records of our visitors, so as not to forget what potion we brewed last time, whether you used it wisely and what effect you achieved.


In the meantime, click here: and add The Witch's Cauldron to your wishlist!

https://cdnb.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/062/465/303/large/harvey-games-blackman-00071.jpg?1683198598

Oh yeah, don't miss the festival, I'll be there too.
Your Bobby, kitty
